But to be clear: if phi is the variance (or precision), then “having them drawn from the same prior” in a pure sense decouples the years completely and you can just run one model for each year. You only need to estimate them jointly if you’re also estimating any parameters in he distribution for phi. Drawing a DAG and spelling out the actual model structure as conditional distribution will help clarify exactly what the model is intended to be.

Finn

